{"title":"2015 IMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/d/3cdf697be1e2fbf30c3a7969525a6f643ded3dc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,\\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"11\" /> of integers satisfies the conditions:<br /><br />\n(i) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/7/e1791b81a3d023133fe250dba8c0f4051760fab4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le a_j\\le2015$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"17\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/6/c86720ccac0c0cbaa59dad0067c7483b51927534.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j\\ge1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />,<br />\n(ii) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/d/f8de68b0bbc2e1ef80f8c38a6471b1e7e8bdf919.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+a_k\\neq \\ell+a_\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"17\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d2730117259f02fae2aa0a24bd05aacc2afe51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le k&lt;\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" />.<br /><br />\nProve that there exist two positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> for which<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36fe4f5dd8887ff6fd9bdb0b381ca76904c191fd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left\\vert\\sum_{j=m+1}^n(a_j-b)\\right\\vert\\le1007^2\\]\" width=\"181\" height=\"54\" />for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b177423f15bdd6e703e67c958f5a75b5ff80c458.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;m\\ge N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" />.<br /><br />\nProposed by Ivan Guo and Ross Atkins, Australia.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can prove the more general statement.<br /><br />\n<u><b>Theorem</b></u> <i>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be a non-negative integer parameter. If given a sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/d/3cdf697be1e2fbf30c3a7969525a6f643ded3dc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,\\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"11\" /> that satisfies the conditions:</i><br />\n(i) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/9/9090acfe84487da931ca48baa22290af49d120b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le a_j \\le T+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"17\" /> <i>for all</i> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/d/f4d90ba6591b9f649820a0e488ed3adf6e7070d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j \\le 1;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" /><br />\n(ii) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/0/4306b87a5e4ce5c50f1e81bc27d0e3a264422a2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+a_k \\ne \\ell+a_\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"17\" /> <i>for all</i> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/3/9b348cf779196fcf19939e3abc520c740ede3716.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le k&lt;\\ell,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /><br />\n<i>then there exist two integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/a/e1a192c8c73dda80c1a06da124d12965179b7203.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le v \\le T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/5/0755192f1ed3b77317e8d60ec40edb5bad5d7a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" />, for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/e/ffee92480cd48390193ffb85cadb6631f3db1354.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left\\vert\\sum_{j=m+1}^n(a_j-(v+1))\\right\\vert\\le (T-v)\\,v \\le \\left(\\frac T 2\\right)^2\\]\" width=\"331\" height=\"54\" />for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b177423f15bdd6e703e67c958f5a75b5ff80c458.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;m\\ge N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" />.</i><br /><br />\n<u><b>Proof</b></u> Consider the set of points on a plane: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/6/7f6435020d6b0d05a344dcf8dab6ded6dfbdecc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{(x,y) \\mid x,y \\in \\mathbb N,\\,y \\le T+1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"227\" height=\"18\" /> (let's call it the <i>base strip</i>). The sequence is represented on it by the subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/b/3fbac1bfae79d7dd1e64e4147805468f28eecfdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{(i,a_i) \\mid i \\in \\mathbb N\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" /> which is painted red. Each line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/6/44695d539b9d5c031d226f37975b8b065313b912.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> of kind <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/d/73d4d19d8d25d19c651e83a48bdac3abd2c459d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317096889b84df0b72bf69ceb4c82208305f1b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" /> is an integer, will be called a <i>carrier</i> line. Note that the condition (ii) states that each carrier line is occupied by at most one red point. Every such line with exactly one red point on it will be called <i>occupied</i> while the rest carriers will be called <i>free</i>.<br />\nFirst we prove that the set of free carriers is finite. Indeed, all the carriers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/6/44695d539b9d5c031d226f37975b8b065313b912.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/f/76fcec797a441f106b08321eb1ea99b7768d0a46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\le n \\le T+m+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"150\" height=\"15\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/9/71905d31548b6ed24dbb52947feab071af5b2d7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\in \\mathbb N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" />, cover the part of the base strip having <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/3/6d35f2e13e25a8572b7169d06220d1b0a1c835af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\le m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, so there are at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> red points lying on them. Thus, the number of free carriers among them is at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99cc5c4a31a8bd65df5004ff9255df9e6682f7ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T+m-m=T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"127\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is arbitrary, the total number of free cariers doesn't exceed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> such that all the carriers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/6/44695d539b9d5c031d226f37975b8b065313b912.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/7/dd7362040c716c07e8446701d27e28ade9837cb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge N+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" /> are occupied.<br />\nNext, take any red point and consider the points on the base strip which are lying on the point's carrier below it (i.e. having strictly greater <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />). Call it the point's <i>trace</i> and paint black. Finally, the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3d21b8b42de64a3afc17c01a99d8eaebc2302d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_x=\\{\\,y \\mid (x,y) \\text { is black}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"191\" height=\"18\" /> will be called a <i>pattern</i>, the number elements <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/9/6b960b223fdf239a38e3e3828ed92d9eed48573f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|P_x|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" /> in it will be called its <i>volume</i> and the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d3962fab414f3e26269d3d356c0c35f5d6f2be1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w_x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"10\" /> of all elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/c/fcc888fa45e97ea325e0ba3269d7efe95a597920.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> will be called its <i>weight</i>.<br />\nNow let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/0/1908ec4913ee37e25ab5d88a8683af23ec72a266.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j&gt;N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" />. Lets track how <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/5/d35c3617166b646206937d658b1e00fb24b30745.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" />, its volume and its weight change when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> increases by 1. Obviously <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2eaeedaad76dac453bc16289bf6591392c558cf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{j+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"17\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/5/d35c3617166b646206937d658b1e00fb24b30745.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" /> plus added <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/0785f19824c8b23ab3dfe000b471994078fdf589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" /> (red point) and shifted down by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />; a point that goes to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> vanishes. This means that the volume doesn't change at all. Indeed, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/8/9f806f4ac6e2e7acbc9947584f84c19be60311d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\notin P_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/152f76ba165d4aa427800f52577a8edad7285092.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" /> or the carrier <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/8/738b075bad551f5cfd7edc8de908bf94f9e76384.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_{j+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"17\" /> will remain unoccupied, so one point always vanishes going to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and exactly one point is added before the shift (it may be the same point). Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be this constant volume. As a pattern never contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/2/702b3f764621a26e2bababbd6f0a872cd6fbb1cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> ranges from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Now it is clearly that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/3/e83760b06fe72598aec683f61b08b01a2cb5a079.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w_{j+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e112d63216392d128e6b9fbe5a09c2d5d6bd48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> plus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/0785f19824c8b23ab3dfe000b471994078fdf589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" /> (red point added) and minus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/2/f82382a5931259deb0c14877d3125014f71d0f4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" /> (all elements are shifted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />), i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/c/2cc2b356bac8b21983804cfd256b90c0c4d6ef3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j-(v+1)=w_{j+1}-w_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b177423f15bdd6e703e67c958f5a75b5ff80c458.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;m\\ge N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/4/db471a0ccd36af0c60486c858d04b73259e3bc24.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{j=m+1}^n(a_j-(v+1))=w_{n+1}-w_{m+1}\\,.\\]\" width=\"287\" height=\"49\" />To finish, it remains to note that the weight ranges from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/0/5506cd215e8924a37ffa395ed0a24e1f991f3333.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2+\\dots+v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"115\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/4/cb4fc94a81aa9725b630e60977fa7de26e57cab6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(T-v+1)+(T-v+2)+\\dots+T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"281\" height=\"18\" />, so its swing is:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d12f35da895ce51fccbeb61665d48af01780c3f7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^v (T-v+i) - \\sum_{i=1}^v i=\\sum_{i=1}^v (T-v)=(T-v)\\,v\\;. \\quad \\blacksquare\\]\" width=\"414\" height=\"47\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO\" title=\"2015 IMO\">2015 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2015 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2015 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017192834\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.050 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 419/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 866/2097152 bytes\nTempl